From: mscharged-port
Subject: Admit original cup game results, knockout and final-round pages and award natives
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a
Classification: temporary explicit original-source diagnostic admission; depends on 0640.

After a cup match the schedule (32) lists the played matchup; pressing it pushes
the original GameResultsScene (33), so the first completed cup game reached a
gated factory case. Once the league phase ends, CycleCupRoundPage and the cup
re-entry push the knockout (34) and final-round (35) pages, whose matchups open
33 as well, and BeginCupAwardPresentation runs the authored award transitions,
which call the cup natives 37 (award rewards popup), 38 (Brick Wall news) and 40
(Golden Boot news). The authored scripts also toggle the cup trophies (7/36) and
can request ShowRoundNews (4).

Under the existing MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_CUP admission, move factory
cases 33-35 and FE natives 4, 7, 36, 37, 38 and 40 into the admitted set,
splitting gated blocks only at case boundaries (online tournament natives 0, 3,
13, 51 and the generic native 6 keep their gates). CupKnockoutScene and
CupFinalRoundsScene read their pointer-button and matchup index from the callback
context word; natively it is a pointer-width value narrowed through
std::intptr_t. Console builds keep the literal casts. Handler bodies, CupManager
progression and every push are unchanged.

